+Reduced-order modeling becomes challenging over broad parameter ranges when parameter variation changes the qualitative dynamics of the system. A single global reduced space and a single reduced dynamical model must then accommodate regimes with different spatial structures and temporal behavior, which can compromise long-horizon autonomous prediction. To address these challenges, we introduce RAL-MoE-ROM, a two-level hierarchical mixture-of-experts ROM that adapts both the reduced representation and the reduced dynamics. The parameter domain is covered by overlapping regime-local parameter regions, each equipped with an independently constructed reduced chart. Within each chart, a hybrid physics--data specialist combines a projected ROM backbone with a structured sparse-MoE correction for unresolved reduced dynamics. At the second level, a parameter-only router selects either one complete local specialist or an applicable adjacent pair of specialists. Since the local reduced coordinates are independent and not componentwise comparable, specialists are advanced
